cementless acetabular cups in total hip arthroplasty: a comparison of two generations at mid-term review introduction &#13;
early versions of cementless acetabular cups in total hip arthroplasty (tha) led to peri-acetabular osteolysis from back-side wear of the polyethylene liner. this unforeseen problem contradicted benefits of using cementless components in younger patients. subsequent generations of components were designed to reduce this problem and its negative effect on the survival of the tha.&#13;
